    "title": "Man shot in Southeast DC, investigation underway - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kaitlyn Dillon ,\n3 hours ago\nWASHINGTON ( DC News Now ) — The Metropolitan Police Department (MPD) is investigating after a man was found shot in Southeast D.C. on Wednesday.\nPolice said officers responded to reports of shots fired at 9:31 p.m. in the 300 block of Parkland Pl. SE.\nDMV politicians, leaders react to government shutdown According to police, a man was found suffering from a gunshot wound nearby in the 300 block of Martin Luther King Jr. Ave.\nHe was transported to the hospital by DC Fire and EMS, conscious and breathing.\nAnyone with information is asked to call (202) 727-9099 or text the Department’s tip line at 50411.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to DC News Now | DC, Virginia, Maryland News, Weather, Traffic, Sports Live.",
